{
  "format": 1,
  "sdk": "1.55",
  "about": "The Steam bridge's allow-list (docs/steam-bridge.md, phase 3), reviewed by hand. A method not listed is refused. mode: call (a round trip; the broker checks as listed), hand (written in bridge_local.c: answered in the game, from the snapshot or fixed), refuse. strings: an input string's longest length in bytes. buffers: an output buffer, the parameter that holds its size and the most the broker accepts. outs: pointers the method writes one value through. ownLobby: CSteamID parameters that must be a lobby the game made or joined this session (LobbyCreated_t or a successful LobbyEnter_t). range: [min, max] for an integer parameter. printable: strings that may hold only printable ASCII. logged: strings the broker writes to its log on every call. p2pPeer: CSteamID parameters that must be one of the game's co-op peers (the backend's lobby and Party peers; a member of a lobby the game joined is not enough, since JoinLobby takes any lobby). refusedStrings: texts a string parameter may not be, ASCII case ignored. inBuffers: bytes the game hands in, the parameter that holds their size and the most the broker accepts. outBytes: a struct the method writes through a pointer, by its size. adjust: integer parameters the broker may change by its own rule before Valve's DLL sees them (BrokerApi.adjust).",
  "callbacks": [
    143,
